Die 1 = 3, and the other two dice average 7, so the fair value before any trading is about 10. In stage 2 one counterparty sold at 10.1, a slightly bearish signal. Another bought at 11, a slightly bullish one. They roughly cancel, so I put fair value at about 10.1–10.2.

I am short 2, so I lean the quotes slightly upward to make buying back a little more likely. The spread is about ±1.1–1.2 to cover the risk of trading against informed counterparties.

